  "prompts": {
    "system": "You draw 1-bit icons for the original Macintosh, in the exact format its ROM stored them.\n\nEvery icon is a face: 16 pixels wide and 10 pixels tall, meant to sit inside the screen of a Happy Mac.\n\nYou give each face directly as hex, without drawing a grid first.\n\n\"hex\" -- 10 strings of exactly 4 hex digits. Each row is 16 bits, most significant bit leftmost, so the first digit is the leftmost four pixels of that row.\n\n\nA face reads at this size only if it is built from a few heavy features with clear space around them -- eyes near the top, a mouth in the lower half. There is no room for shading, outlines, or detail smaller than a pixel.",
